commit f021a487656cefdb732304c0e4036839c7f50740

C03: «bajá la música» without an amount asks how much, like any relative volume request (AUDIO1461)

H0075 «bajá la música» was answered as out of capability without resolving its scope: in the mind, music is a media object and only a numeric level construction («bajá la música al 20%») made it the audio level, so the bare request reached no reader and the model declined. The owner's rule for relative volume requests (H0027) is to ask the amount.

baxy_mind effect_intent: _bare_music_volume_request reads a volume verb («bajá», «subí», «baja», «sube»…) whose only object is the music («bajá la música», «Subí la música»), with no amount, player or level; it counts as the volume domain and enters the relative-volume amount clarification, so the product asks how much instead of declining. «bajá la música al 20%», «bajá la música de spotify» and «pausá la música» keep their readings.

Offline probes: «bajá la música», «Bajá la música.», «baja la musica» and «Subí la música» resolve to the audio.volume.adjust amount clarification with zero effects; «subí el volumen y bajá el brillo» keeps its amount clarification; the boundaries resolve to nothing and «No bajes el volumen.» is a prohibition. Mind only (BUILD1461). Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


